WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.633
- Most people have a stressful life.

00:00:02.633 --> 00:00:05.628
And if you look at stress,
stress happens as a result

00:00:05.628 --> 00:00:07.668
of things not fitting your pictures.

00:00:07.668 --> 00:00:09.418
Perfection is the lowest standard.

00:00:09.418 --> 00:00:11.505
And the reason it's the lowest standard

00:00:11.505 --> 00:00:12.680
is because it's unattainable.

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:13.513
Failure?

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:15.356
Failure is not taking your step.

00:00:15.356 --> 00:00:17.225
Failure is not picking up the bat

00:00:17.225 --> 00:00:18.973
and swinging it at life.

00:00:18.973 --> 00:00:20.973
Failure is getting to the end of this game

00:00:20.973 --> 00:00:23.436
and regretting what we didn't do.

00:00:23.436 --> 00:00:25.710
I'm a born entrepreneur.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.324
I've built several dozen companies,

00:00:27.324 --> 00:00:29.388
half of which before the age of 30.

00:00:29.388 --> 00:00:31.487
I'm a best-selling author, philosopher

00:00:31.487 --> 00:00:33.282
and explorer of consciousness.

00:00:33.282 --> 00:00:34.978
My name is Peter Sage,

00:00:34.978 --> 00:00:37.791
and these are my 10 rules for success.

00:00:37.791 --> 00:00:40.560
(exploding swoosh)

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.310
(powerful music)

00:00:50.528 --> 00:00:51.995
Probably the most important
way to encourage yourself

00:00:51.995 --> 00:00:55.245
to work harder is to increase your why.

00:00:57.862 --> 00:00:59.324
You see, the psychological fact

00:00:59.324 --> 00:01:00.958
that people do things for reasons,

00:01:00.958 --> 00:01:03.002
now, they may not be your reasons,

00:01:03.002 --> 00:01:04.037
and they may not be my reasons,

00:01:04.037 --> 00:01:06.487
but everybody does things for reasons.

00:01:06.487 --> 00:01:08.537
And so what you do when
you're working hard

00:01:08.537 --> 00:01:09.946
or you're working on a project,

00:01:09.946 --> 00:01:11.626
you're doing it because
there's a reason for it.

00:01:11.626 --> 00:01:13.767
Now if your motivation is low,

00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:16.377
it's because your reason, the
reason that you're doing it

00:01:16.377 --> 00:01:18.522
doesn't resonate at a high level.

00:01:18.522 --> 00:01:20.718
So how do you increase your why?

00:01:20.718 --> 00:01:23.017
Well, one the ways that I found

00:01:23.017 --> 00:01:25.708
is by focusing on what is the outcome

00:01:25.708 --> 00:01:27.418
of what it is that you're doing,

00:01:27.418 --> 00:01:29.946
and how can that serve beyond you

00:01:29.946 --> 00:01:32.222
to people that you care about

00:01:32.222 --> 00:01:33.592
or the world at large?

00:01:33.592 --> 00:01:37.529
People can be motivated by
themselves up to a point.

00:01:37.529 --> 00:01:40.618
But when you start motivating yourself

00:01:40.618 --> 00:01:42.359
because of what you can contribute,

00:01:42.359 --> 00:01:44.902
you tap into a deeper level of motivation.

00:01:44.902 --> 00:01:47.719
You know, it's a fact, if you
look at the New York Marathon,

00:01:47.719 --> 00:01:49.350
The Boston Marathon, The London Marathon,

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:50.395
there's more people

00:01:50.395 --> 00:01:53.901
that run those marathons
for the first time,

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:57.919
running for other people,
causes, charities.

00:01:57.919 --> 00:01:58.752
And then think about

00:01:58.752 --> 00:02:00.681
how much it would take
to motivate yourself

00:02:00.681 --> 00:02:02.378
if you've never ran a marathon before

00:02:02.378 --> 00:02:03.608
to go and train for one.

00:02:03.608 --> 00:02:07.033
And getting up when you
need to do a 20K, or

00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:10.330
a 15-mile training run and it's
cold and wet and miserable,

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.316
and you haven't eaten
properly and you're tired,

00:02:12.316 --> 00:02:14.011
but you got to go do it anyway.

00:02:14.011 --> 00:02:15.590
If we're doing it for ourselves,

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:17.803
a lot of the time we can quit.

00:02:17.803 --> 00:02:19.168
But if we're doing it for others,

00:02:19.168 --> 00:02:21.105
there's something that compels us.

00:02:21.105 --> 00:02:23.165
If you've got to get up early

00:02:23.165 --> 00:02:24.976
to go get yourself to a certain place,

00:02:24.976 --> 00:02:27.797
and you're not feeling
motivated, it's hard.

00:02:27.797 --> 00:02:29.091
But if you've got to get up and go,

00:02:29.091 --> 00:02:31.076
because your boss will
fire you if you don't,

00:02:31.076 --> 00:02:32.852
or you got to pick the
kids up from the airport,

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:34.581
there's a different reason.

00:02:34.581 --> 00:02:38.100
So focus on what it is that is your why.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:40.004
And checking, 6is it self-serving,

00:02:40.004 --> 00:02:41.664
which is limiting in its power?

00:02:41.664 --> 00:02:43.798
Or is it more ethnocentric,

00:02:43.798 --> 00:02:45.043
whereby I'm doing it for a reason.

00:02:45.043 --> 00:02:46.702
And find a reason to be able to contribute

00:02:46.702 --> 00:02:48.208
with what it is that you're doing.

00:02:48.208 --> 00:02:49.890
Over time, and especially
in personal development,

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:51.764
many people have put different emphasis

00:02:51.764 --> 00:02:52.980
on different buzzwords,

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:56.033
things like persistence, and
desire, and determination,

00:02:56.033 --> 00:02:58.451
words that usually have a
lot of strength behind them.

00:02:58.451 --> 00:03:00.563
Words that really have a connotation to

00:03:00.563 --> 00:03:02.482
being able to battle through.

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:05.628
And while things like desire,
persistence, determination,

00:03:05.628 --> 00:03:07.370
et cetera, are very useful,

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:09.912
they're useful for when
we go through obstacles,

00:03:09.912 --> 00:03:12.687
when we require an
immediate injection of force

00:03:12.687 --> 00:03:15.665
to try and break through
certain levels of limitation.

00:03:15.665 --> 00:03:18.727
In other words, if we are sitting
there as a victim of life,

00:03:18.727 --> 00:03:21.525
and we want to be able to break
out and take charge of our

00:03:21.525 --> 00:03:25.937
own circumstances, words
like persistence and desire,

00:03:25.937 --> 00:03:29.126
and being able to break
through, are valuable words.

00:03:29.126 --> 00:03:32.565
But I'd like to give you an
insight into a word that I think

00:03:32.565 --> 00:03:34.456
is far more powerful.

00:03:34.456 --> 00:03:36.904
And this word has been given
to us throughout the ages

00:03:36.904 --> 00:03:39.300
by prophets, scholars, religious teachers,

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.479
spiritual masters, consistently,

00:03:41.479 --> 00:03:44.165
since the dawn of written civilization,

00:03:44.165 --> 00:03:47.079
and that is the word surrender.

00:03:47.079 --> 00:03:50.980
The word surrender is
inherent into letting go

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:52.743
of resistance.

00:03:52.743 --> 00:03:55.826
If you think of, for example, stress,

00:03:57.016 --> 00:03:59.478
most people have a stressful life.

00:03:59.478 --> 00:04:02.438
And if you look at stress,
stress happens as a result

00:04:02.438 --> 00:04:04.262
of things not fitting your picture.

00:04:04.262 --> 00:04:06.215
In other words, if you take
the scientific definition,

00:04:06.215 --> 00:04:09.222
it's two objects going against each other

00:04:09.222 --> 00:04:12.123
with opposing forces
in opposite directions.

00:04:12.123 --> 00:04:14.598
Not like, for example,
if you take a dance,

00:04:14.598 --> 00:04:15.788
and I'm doing Salsa dance,

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:18.075
and I take a lady on an outside turn,

00:04:18.075 --> 00:04:20.095
then we're going in opposite directions.

00:04:20.095 --> 00:04:22.092
And that's fine, you're
going with the flow.

00:04:22.092 --> 00:04:24.112
But if she's trying to
move on an inside turn,

00:04:24.112 --> 00:04:27.085
and I'm doing an outside
turn, you have a friction,

00:04:27.085 --> 00:04:29.488
a resistance, and that's going
to end up in a broken wrist.

00:04:29.488 --> 00:04:33.208
So being able to surrender at the point

00:04:33.208 --> 00:04:35.305
has a different connotation.

00:04:35.305 --> 00:04:36.665
So let's look into it a little more.

00:04:36.665 --> 00:04:38.677
If we're trying to force
our way through life,

00:04:38.677 --> 00:04:41.575
battling through,
surrender is not an option

00:04:41.575 --> 00:04:42.763
for most people.

00:04:42.763 --> 00:04:45.547
But if we start to look deeper
and know that the wisdom

00:04:45.547 --> 00:04:49.033
behind the intelligence
that governs a lot of

00:04:49.033 --> 00:04:51.222
the flow of the river of life,

00:04:51.222 --> 00:04:52.696
let's call in the current of life,

00:04:52.696 --> 00:04:55.030
has an innate level of intelligence

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:58.718
that goes beyond what we
can comprehend consciously.

00:04:58.718 --> 00:04:59.719
How do I know that?

00:04:59.719 --> 00:05:01.467
Very simple, cut your
finger and consciously

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.019
try to stop it from healing.

00:05:03.019 --> 00:05:05.403
There's something smarter
than us that's at work there.

00:05:05.403 --> 00:05:09.327
Whereas, if we were to
surrender to the wisdom

00:05:09.327 --> 00:05:12.155
of the current of the river,
if we were to surrender

00:05:12.155 --> 00:05:15.405
to that level of intelligence, then eh,

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:19.565
what generally happens is that
a solution to our problems

00:05:19.565 --> 00:05:21.483
will present itself.

00:05:21.483 --> 00:05:23.642
If you want to flow with
the wisdom of the current,

00:05:23.642 --> 00:05:26.603
know that if life takes a
left turn, which it has to,

00:05:26.603 --> 00:05:28.699
you look at any river from the air,

00:05:28.699 --> 00:05:31.653
and regardless of the
topography, regardless

00:05:31.653 --> 00:05:32.919
of where you are on the planet,

00:05:32.919 --> 00:05:35.113
they all follow the
same pattern, they wind.

00:05:35.113 --> 00:05:36.924
Just like the roads around
me in the background here,

00:05:36.924 --> 00:05:39.095
they all wind in a different pattern.

00:05:39.095 --> 00:05:42.297
So if you have a goal in mind,

00:05:42.297 --> 00:05:45.387
and you've gone through persistence,

00:05:45.387 --> 00:05:46.939
you've gone through determination,

00:05:46.939 --> 00:05:49.834
and yet still struggling, try surrendering

00:05:49.834 --> 00:05:52.309
to the inevitably of it happening

00:05:52.309 --> 00:05:54.602
by flowing with the wisdom of the current.

00:05:54.602 --> 00:05:56.824
And if you do that, and you tap into

00:05:56.824 --> 00:05:58.345
that innate level of wisdom,

00:05:58.345 --> 00:06:00.167
that has been passed
down through the ages,

00:06:00.167 --> 00:06:04.277
you'll start to see surrender
as alignment with the current,

00:06:04.277 --> 00:06:05.879
rather than resisting it.

00:06:05.879 --> 00:06:07.664
If we understand that for
the majority of people

00:06:07.664 --> 00:06:09.776
on the planet, money is
nothing more than a reflection

00:06:09.776 --> 00:06:11.407
of the value that they've added,

00:06:11.407 --> 00:06:15.122
then we start to understand
that what has to come first

00:06:15.122 --> 00:06:17.978
is the value, not going
around chasing money.

00:06:17.978 --> 00:06:20.078
If you chase money,
you'll chase your tail,

00:06:20.078 --> 00:06:22.285
because you're chasing the
consequence of something

00:06:22.285 --> 00:06:23.933
that hasn't happened yet.

00:06:23.933 --> 00:06:24.975
Does that make sense?

00:06:24.975 --> 00:06:27.006
So if you look at it under that context,

00:06:27.006 --> 00:06:29.646
then how do you start a
business with no money?

00:06:29.646 --> 00:06:31.939
Well, you don't ask yourself,
"Where do I get money?"

00:06:31.939 --> 00:06:33.697
You ask yourself a better question.

00:06:33.697 --> 00:06:36.973
You say, "Where is it
that I can add value?

00:06:36.973 --> 00:06:38.562
"How can I add value?

00:06:38.562 --> 00:06:41.950
"What is it that I can
contribute that would

00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:43.919
"cause somebody to be
able to give me what it is

00:06:43.919 --> 00:06:46.657
"that I want, without just
shelling out a wad of cash."

00:06:46.657 --> 00:06:47.490
That's the easy way.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:50.274
All money is an arbitrary
medium of exchange

00:06:50.274 --> 00:06:52.688
to measure different levels of value,

00:06:52.688 --> 00:06:53.884
that's pretty much it.

00:06:53.884 --> 00:06:55.997
So if we don't have access to money,

00:06:55.997 --> 00:06:57.558
then what we have to
do is come up with ways

00:06:57.558 --> 00:07:01.051
we can add value, and therefore
we shortcut the process.

00:07:01.051 --> 00:07:03.962
One of the patterns that
I'm noticing here, Eric,

00:07:03.962 --> 00:07:06.763
in a lot of consistent ways
with new entrepreneurs,

00:07:06.763 --> 00:07:09.435
is that they're covering up their lack

00:07:09.435 --> 00:07:13.046
of ability to handle
uncertainty by doing research,

00:07:13.046 --> 00:07:16.158
under the guise of chasing perfectionism.

00:07:16.158 --> 00:07:17.332
- Yeah.

00:07:17.332 --> 00:07:18.165
- Right?

00:07:18.165 --> 00:07:19.000
That's like saying, well,
listen, I'm going to read

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:21.891
all the books on darts that I can read

00:07:21.891 --> 00:07:25.214
so that my first dart is
going to be a bullseye.

00:07:25.214 --> 00:07:26.934
- Yeah.
- That doesn't work.

00:07:26.934 --> 00:07:30.299
Get up, stand up to
the plate, or the oche,

00:07:30.299 --> 00:07:32.505
throw the dart, and the
first one may miss the board.

00:07:32.505 --> 00:07:35.040
But then you adjust, you
throw the second one,

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:36.646
it gets a little closer,
you throw the third one,

00:07:36.646 --> 00:07:37.647
it gets a little closer.

00:07:37.647 --> 00:07:40.325
Eventually, you're going
to be getting bullseyes,

00:07:40.325 --> 00:07:42.163
because you're used to throwing,

00:07:42.163 --> 00:07:43.831
not used to reading books on darts.

00:07:43.831 --> 00:07:45.042
- Your experience.

00:07:45.042 --> 00:07:46.756
Your experience is getting
better on this one.

00:07:46.756 --> 00:07:47.589
Yeah, so.

00:07:47.589 --> 00:07:48.960
- See, if I'm trying to be perfect,

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:52.303
then to all you perfectionist
people out there,

00:07:52.303 --> 00:07:53.136
listen to me.

00:07:53.136 --> 00:07:54.548
Again, another one of my mentors,

00:07:54.548 --> 00:07:56.697
I've spent on many years
with, Tony Robbins, right,

00:07:56.697 --> 00:07:58.821
will tell you perfection
is the lowest standard.

00:07:58.821 --> 00:08:00.907
And the reason it's
the the lowest standard

00:08:00.907 --> 00:08:03.253
is because it's unattainable.

00:08:03.253 --> 00:08:04.808
So why are you trying to be perfect?

00:08:04.808 --> 00:08:08.621
By being perfect, you
guarantee you never will be.

00:08:08.621 --> 00:08:10.427
- Most people try to be perfect,

00:08:10.427 --> 00:08:12.449
try do this exactly--

00:08:12.449 --> 00:08:14.231
- Now, most people are
afraid of being imperfect,

00:08:14.231 --> 00:08:15.933
exactly.
- But I think this is go

00:08:15.933 --> 00:08:18.511
to the procrastination problem.

00:08:18.511 --> 00:08:20.205
They procrastinate or--

00:08:20.205 --> 00:08:21.232
- Under the guise of research.

00:08:21.232 --> 00:08:22.286
- Yeah.

00:08:22.286 --> 00:08:24.529
- Well, I'll just do
two more focus groups,

00:08:24.529 --> 00:08:27.869
or I'll just like do another hours surfing

00:08:27.869 --> 00:08:30.625
to see if there's any other
ideas I can benchmark.

00:08:30.625 --> 00:08:32.193
No, shut up, do your

00:08:32.193 --> 00:08:33.026
research--
- That's not good, yeah.

00:08:33.026 --> 00:08:34.865
- Limit it, get in the
game, swing the bat,

00:08:34.865 --> 00:08:37.328
then reassess, but at
least you're in the game.

00:08:37.328 --> 00:08:39.408
Set yourself up to win.

00:08:39.408 --> 00:08:43.738
Now, this may sound easy, but
let me give you some insight

00:08:43.738 --> 00:08:45.246
into brain chemistry.

00:08:45.246 --> 00:08:48.057
Now one of my good friends, Dave Asprey,

00:08:48.057 --> 00:08:50.157
from the Bulletproof
team, yeah, amazing man,

00:08:50.157 --> 00:08:52.283
shared this with me, and that is that

00:08:52.283 --> 00:08:55.857
the brain, although it's
1/50th of the body weight,

00:08:55.857 --> 00:08:59.087
takes up 20% of the calories.

00:08:59.087 --> 00:09:01.823
20% of the energy in your body
goes to running your brain.

00:09:01.823 --> 00:09:04.825
Now if that energy is low, guess what?

00:09:04.825 --> 00:09:06.456
You feel demotivated.

00:09:06.456 --> 00:09:09.034
And a lot of the time, people
try and rely on willpower.

00:09:09.034 --> 00:09:11.405
But willpower isn't on demand.

00:09:11.405 --> 00:09:15.734
Willpower has cycles based
upon whether your brain

00:09:15.734 --> 00:09:17.452
is being fed the energy it needs.

00:09:17.452 --> 00:09:20.135
So if you are feeling down, and think,

00:09:20.135 --> 00:09:22.407
"Ah, I was going to commit
to that, but I can't,

00:09:22.407 --> 00:09:23.607
"I'm just not in the mood."

00:09:23.607 --> 00:09:25.139
And you don't want to work harder,

00:09:25.139 --> 00:09:28.310
then first things first, go
check your brain chemistry,

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:31.895
get yourself some fast
sugars into the diet,

00:09:31.895 --> 00:09:35.122
get some high quality
brain fuel to be able to

00:09:35.122 --> 00:09:37.320
perk yourself back up at
that level then go do it.

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:39.595
Another great way of
setting yourself up to win,

00:09:39.595 --> 00:09:41.869
is that when you're in
the mood to do something,

00:09:41.869 --> 00:09:45.528
prepare something for when you're going

00:09:45.528 --> 00:09:47.103
to be doing the project.

00:09:47.103 --> 00:09:48.779
In other words, I'll give you an example.

00:09:48.779 --> 00:09:50.648
If you go to bed at night,

00:09:50.648 --> 00:09:52.702
put your gym kit at the bottom of the bed

00:09:52.702 --> 00:09:54.294
if you're going to the gym in the morning.

00:09:54.294 --> 00:09:56.300
Research has shown, if you get out of bed,

00:09:56.300 --> 00:09:58.520
and that gym kit is more
than 20 seconds away,

00:09:58.520 --> 00:10:01.579
you're not likely to make it
if you're not in the mood.

00:10:01.579 --> 00:10:03.610
But if your gym kit is
at the foot of the bed,

00:10:03.610 --> 00:10:05.514
and you get out and the first
thing you do is put it on,

00:10:05.514 --> 00:10:06.880
you're ahead of the game.

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:08.684
Set yourself up to win.

00:10:08.684 --> 00:10:11.247
So when I'm in the mood
and I am energized,

00:10:11.247 --> 00:10:13.386
my brain chemistry's
high, and I'm associated

00:10:13.386 --> 00:10:14.559
to what I'm doing,

00:10:14.559 --> 00:10:16.749
do something in that moment to take action

00:10:16.749 --> 00:10:18.843
towards setting yourself
up for when you know

00:10:18.843 --> 00:10:20.898
predictably that cycle's going to dip.

00:10:20.898 --> 00:10:23.185
'Cause you can't be in
uptime all the while.

00:10:23.185 --> 00:10:25.074
That's a superhuman myth.

00:10:25.074 --> 00:10:26.412
Well, here's the tip.

00:10:26.412 --> 00:10:28.337
It's not looking for more sales,

00:10:28.337 --> 00:10:30.621
it's not getting up
earlier and making calls.

00:10:30.621 --> 00:10:32.043
It's not knocking on doors.

00:10:32.043 --> 00:10:36.210
The fastest way to make money
is to raise your self-worth.

00:10:37.197 --> 00:10:38.986
How do you raise your self-worth?

00:10:38.986 --> 00:10:40.636
Check your peer group.

00:10:40.636 --> 00:10:42.608
If you upgrade your peer group,

00:10:42.608 --> 00:10:45.673
you'll upgrade your
self-worth, case closed.

00:10:45.673 --> 00:10:47.612
What do I mean by that?

00:10:47.612 --> 00:10:49.335
Well, if you hang around
with 10 drug addicts,

00:10:49.335 --> 00:10:50.445
I've got news for you.

00:10:50.445 --> 00:10:52.620
The law of conformity says
you'll likely become the 11th.

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:55.325
If you hang around with
10 highly motivated

00:10:55.325 --> 00:10:58.123
self-made multimillionaires
that are up and busy,

00:10:58.123 --> 00:10:59.661
on purpose, with something, and inspired

00:10:59.661 --> 00:11:03.441
to go out and create value,
you're likely become the 11th.

00:11:03.441 --> 00:11:08.159
You see, raise your self-esteem,
trade your peer group,

00:11:08.159 --> 00:11:09.437
and ask yourself a question.

00:11:09.437 --> 00:11:10.578
How can I add value?

00:11:10.578 --> 00:11:12.628
And all of a sudden, you look
over your shoulder one day

00:11:12.628 --> 00:11:14.310
and think, "Wow, where
did that money come from?"

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:17.084
Because now you're focusing
on what you can give,

00:11:17.084 --> 00:11:19.491
which is the by-product
or a consequence of that

00:11:19.491 --> 00:11:20.820
is money coming in.

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:22.660
Rather than sitting in front at the fire,

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:24.362
and bitching about the
fact that it's cold,

00:11:24.362 --> 00:11:25.621
and if only you had some heat,

00:11:25.621 --> 00:11:27.344
you'll go outside and fetch some wood.

00:11:27.344 --> 00:11:28.436
That doesn't work.

00:11:28.436 --> 00:11:29.733
You want more money?

00:11:29.733 --> 00:11:31.141
Become a person of value.

00:11:31.141 --> 00:11:33.974
Upgrade your self-worth,
mix with the people

00:11:33.974 --> 00:11:36.133
that already have what
it is that you want,

00:11:36.133 --> 00:11:37.573
contribute in adding value,

00:11:37.573 --> 00:11:39.545
and I guarantee money won't be far behind.

00:11:39.545 --> 00:11:41.962
If you are able to understand

00:11:43.064 --> 00:11:46.826
that you get to choose the
meaning of what happens,

00:11:46.826 --> 00:11:51.433
you get to take responsibility
for your data-processing

00:11:51.433 --> 00:11:52.964
of the five senses.

00:11:52.964 --> 00:11:55.800
Two men sat behind
prison bars, one saw mud,

00:11:55.800 --> 00:11:57.136
the other saw stars.

00:11:57.136 --> 00:12:00.165
The condition is identical
in both scenarios.

00:12:00.165 --> 00:12:02.870
How one chooses to
interpret that condition

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:05.817
determines whether or
not you go off on a track

00:12:05.817 --> 00:12:08.650
towards empowerment, or
whether you go off on a track

00:12:08.650 --> 00:12:10.324
that becomes a self-fulfilling prophecy

00:12:10.324 --> 00:12:12.434
of more stress and resentment

00:12:12.434 --> 00:12:14.000
with your current life condition.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:16.048
If you've ever had a
relationship with somebody,

00:12:16.048 --> 00:12:17.909
or an intimate relationships
where, for example,

00:12:17.909 --> 00:12:19.154
they left you.

00:12:19.154 --> 00:12:22.404
Same scenario, two different
ways of looking at it.

00:12:22.404 --> 00:12:23.710
One, you can turn around and say,

00:12:23.710 --> 00:12:25.452
"Well, I'm clearly no
good, so they left me."

00:12:25.452 --> 00:12:27.408
Or you can say, "Well,
thank God they went,

00:12:27.408 --> 00:12:29.126
"so they made room for
somebody who's right.

00:12:29.126 --> 00:12:30.787
"Next!"

00:12:30.787 --> 00:12:33.398
Now just stay with that
example for a second.

00:12:33.398 --> 00:12:36.731
If you suddenly go out and a year later,

00:12:38.083 --> 00:12:39.779
six months down the line, whatever it is,

00:12:39.779 --> 00:12:40.711
if I were on the first scenario,

00:12:40.711 --> 00:12:42.090
"I'm no good, so they left me."

00:12:42.090 --> 00:12:43.813
And that's my belief, that's all it is,

00:12:43.813 --> 00:12:45.105
has nothing to do with the actual event,

00:12:45.105 --> 00:12:47.392
the event is the event.

00:12:47.392 --> 00:12:50.734
But if I'm processing my data management

00:12:50.734 --> 00:12:54.209
through the filter or the
belief, or the choice of

00:12:54.209 --> 00:12:55.695
"I'm no good, so they left me."

00:12:55.695 --> 00:12:58.438
Because that's my story,
that's my upbringing,

00:12:58.438 --> 00:13:00.829
that's my social conditioning,
that's my parents,

00:13:00.829 --> 00:13:02.201
that's my fill-in-the-blank.

00:13:02.201 --> 00:13:03.815
We all have a story, my friends.

00:13:03.815 --> 00:13:07.100
Then, the next time I go to meet somebody,

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:09.131
or I'm introduced to somebody,

00:13:09.131 --> 00:13:11.103
what are my default thoughts?

00:13:11.103 --> 00:13:13.869
"Oh, I wonder if this person
thinks I'm good enough."

00:13:13.869 --> 00:13:15.819
Now if that's your starting place,

00:13:15.819 --> 00:13:18.113
I can predict what's going to
happen over the next two dates,

00:13:18.113 --> 00:13:20.461
if you get to number
two, that is. (laughs)

00:13:20.461 --> 00:13:24.457
Whereas, if you turn around,
if we rewind six months before,

00:13:24.457 --> 00:13:25.630
and you say, "Next!

00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:27.185
"Oh, yeah, thank goodness that person went

00:13:27.185 --> 00:13:28.840
"so they made room for
somebody who's right."

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:31.065
And that is your default
level of processing,

00:13:31.065 --> 00:13:32.210
'cause it's a choice.

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:34.591
Then next time you meet somebody,

00:13:34.591 --> 00:13:38.558
what is your default level
of being able to interact?

00:13:38.558 --> 00:13:41.078
Well, yeah, I wonder if
this person's going to be

00:13:41.078 --> 00:13:43.172
fortunate enough to spend
to spend some time with me.

00:13:43.172 --> 00:13:44.881
And as long as it comes
from a place of authenticity

00:13:44.881 --> 00:13:47.584
not arrogance, because
you're feeling empowered,

00:13:47.584 --> 00:13:50.100
not disempowered, yeah, your second date's

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:52.341
going to be a very different experience.

00:13:52.341 --> 00:13:53.536
You understand what I'm saying?

00:13:53.536 --> 00:13:57.655
We create our interpretation
of meaning of the world,

00:13:57.655 --> 00:14:00.485
irrespective of the
external circumstances.

00:14:00.485 --> 00:14:02.627
If I'm going to do business with somebody,

00:14:02.627 --> 00:14:05.188
I want to do business with somebody I like

00:14:05.188 --> 00:14:06.441
and somebody I trust.

00:14:06.441 --> 00:14:08.165
We want to be in business
with those people.

00:14:08.165 --> 00:14:13.141
So what does it take to like
somebody and trust somebody?

00:14:13.141 --> 00:14:17.267
If you're putting on some
level of fake rapport skills,

00:14:17.267 --> 00:14:19.206
because you've learnt some NLP technique

00:14:19.206 --> 00:14:21.956
on how to be closely in alignment

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:25.497
with somebody who's visual
versus auditory or kinesthetic,

00:14:25.497 --> 00:14:27.307
then that's going to get you in the door.

00:14:27.307 --> 00:14:31.692
But there's an inherent
level of falseness with that.

00:14:31.692 --> 00:14:35.859
Sincerity comes from a level
of empathy and intention

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:41.642
that is there to express who
you are to serve your client.

00:14:41.642 --> 00:14:44.137
If you don't have the
ability to respect your time,

00:14:44.137 --> 00:14:45.258
nobody else will.

00:14:45.258 --> 00:14:46.091
- Yeah.

00:14:46.091 --> 00:14:49.234
- Now it doesn't mean to say
you got to be a jerk about it.

00:14:49.234 --> 00:14:52.177
There is something respectful

00:14:52.177 --> 00:14:54.228
about people who own their own time.

00:14:54.228 --> 00:14:56.757
And if somebody calls me and says,

00:14:56.757 --> 00:15:00.389
or goes through my secretary
saying they want a meeting,

00:15:00.389 --> 00:15:03.444
nobody gets access to time
with me unless they send

00:15:03.444 --> 00:15:05.042
an agenda in advance,

00:15:05.042 --> 00:15:07.398
and we assess it as being
mutually beneficial.

00:15:07.398 --> 00:15:08.231
- Yeah.

00:15:08.231 --> 00:15:11.129
- Otherwise, I'm not
going to be able to focus

00:15:11.129 --> 00:15:13.540
on what my mission is, I'm going
to be serving everybody else's

00:15:13.540 --> 00:15:15.715
Now, you see, many people avoid that

00:15:15.715 --> 00:15:16.917
because they have a fear of rejection.

00:15:16.917 --> 00:15:18.041
They don't like saying no.

00:15:18.041 --> 00:15:19.320
"I don't want to hurt
somebody's feelings."

00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:20.945
- Yeah, this is the main problem.

00:15:20.945 --> 00:15:23.871
I cannot just give the
time to someone else.

00:15:23.871 --> 00:15:26.057
- But that's not about
them, that's about you

00:15:26.057 --> 00:15:28.704
being driven by the good opinion of others

00:15:28.704 --> 00:15:30.074
and scared of rejection,

00:15:30.074 --> 00:15:33.209
because you think it's a person sop.

00:15:33.209 --> 00:15:36.030
But if you own yourself,
and you own your truth,

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:37.684
it's very easy to say no to people.

00:15:37.684 --> 00:15:40.109
It's like, I've employed
hundreds of people over the years

00:15:40.109 --> 00:15:41.399
in different businesses.

00:15:41.399 --> 00:15:43.543
And sometimes you've
got to let go of people.

00:15:43.543 --> 00:15:47.355
And I don't see that as ruining their day,

00:15:47.355 --> 00:15:48.987
I see that as giving them an opportunity

00:15:48.987 --> 00:15:51.465
to be in a job that's
better suited to them.

00:15:51.465 --> 00:15:52.457
Now, they may not see that at the time

00:15:52.457 --> 00:15:53.771
when they're focusing on scarcity.

00:15:53.771 --> 00:15:55.158
- Improve themselves, yeah.

00:15:55.158 --> 00:15:57.941
- Or the fact that they
don't have wages next week.

00:15:57.941 --> 00:15:58.774
- Yeah.

00:15:58.774 --> 00:16:01.179
- But, I don't want them being in a place

00:16:01.179 --> 00:16:03.139
where they don't fit.

00:16:03.139 --> 00:16:04.880
And if they don't have the
courage to recognize that

00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:07.216
and leave it, then I'm the
guy that needs to help.

00:16:07.216 --> 00:16:08.049
And three months down the line,

00:16:08.049 --> 00:16:09.512
when they hopefully get a better job,

00:16:09.512 --> 00:16:11.246
or find themselves in a better position,

00:16:11.246 --> 00:16:13.089
and if they look back at the time when

00:16:13.089 --> 00:16:14.928
the transition point was there,

00:16:14.928 --> 00:16:17.187
they thank me for having the
courage to make that decision

00:16:17.187 --> 00:16:19.084
for them if they didn't.

00:16:19.084 --> 00:16:21.453
So I don't need the good opinion of others

00:16:21.453 --> 00:16:25.180
if I'm walking my truth, and
I'm always coming from a place

00:16:25.180 --> 00:16:26.816
of wanting to serve.

00:16:26.816 --> 00:16:30.064
It's not an egocentric position.

00:16:30.064 --> 00:16:33.591
I'm not trying to say,
"Well, screw you, my time's

00:16:33.591 --> 00:16:35.112
"more important than yours."

00:16:35.112 --> 00:16:36.952
I'm saying, "Well, right now,

00:16:36.952 --> 00:16:38.473
"this doesn't serve our outcome."

00:16:38.473 --> 00:16:41.845
It's got to be mutually beneficial.

00:16:41.845 --> 00:16:45.259
And if you need some time
and this is a project

00:16:45.259 --> 00:16:49.210
you want my advice on, then,
A, I have an hourly rate

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:50.535
that you can book.

00:16:50.535 --> 00:16:52.346
But if you're looking for free advice,

00:16:52.346 --> 00:16:54.724
I have a huge amount of
information out there on YouTube

00:16:54.724 --> 00:16:57.122
that I do so that people
that can't afford my time

00:16:57.122 --> 00:16:59.043
can have access to some benefit.

00:16:59.043 --> 00:17:01.142
But, other than that, I'm very sorry,

00:17:01.142 --> 00:17:02.978
my time and my mission isn't aligned

00:17:02.978 --> 00:17:04.298
with where yours is right now.

00:17:04.298 --> 00:17:07.263
Now if there's one area that
I see stopping so many people

00:17:07.263 --> 00:17:09.920
from living their dream,
from fulfilling the potential

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:12.754
that they were born to
fulfill, it is getting over

00:17:12.754 --> 00:17:14.509
the fear of failure.

00:17:14.509 --> 00:17:15.611
So how do you do that?

00:17:15.611 --> 00:17:17.839
How do you take that fear
and rip it out by the roots

00:17:17.839 --> 00:17:20.738
and throw it away so it
never bothers you again?

00:17:20.738 --> 00:17:24.498
You start to understand what
fear of failure is actually is,

00:17:24.498 --> 00:17:28.434
'cause for many people, all
it is is being sucker punched

00:17:28.434 --> 00:17:31.110
by the good opinion of
other people caring about

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:32.271
what they think.

00:17:32.271 --> 00:17:34.720
You know how often that keeps up down?

00:17:34.720 --> 00:17:36.949
Do you know how much of a life is wasted

00:17:36.949 --> 00:17:39.442
caring about what we think
other people are thinking?

00:17:39.442 --> 00:17:42.226
And the reality is this.

00:17:42.226 --> 00:17:47.073
You start as the number one
A-list actor in your movie

00:17:47.073 --> 00:17:48.421
called Your Life.

00:17:48.421 --> 00:17:49.699
Do you not?

00:17:49.699 --> 00:17:52.048
Which means that everybody else
either is a supporting cast,

00:17:52.048 --> 00:17:55.333
or a film extra, in the
movie of your life, correct?

00:17:55.333 --> 00:17:57.281
But what does that really mean?

00:17:57.281 --> 00:17:59.379
We walk around thinking people look at us

00:17:59.379 --> 00:18:01.454
as the star in our movie, but they don't.

00:18:01.454 --> 00:18:03.791
Everybody else is living the same dream,

00:18:03.791 --> 00:18:06.171
they're walking around in
the star of their own movie,

00:18:06.171 --> 00:18:08.511
and we're just a film
extra in their movie.

00:18:08.511 --> 00:18:11.937
So if we stop taking the actions

00:18:11.937 --> 00:18:14.096
that we think we will
lead towards success,

00:18:14.096 --> 00:18:16.640
because we think we're worried
about what the good opinion

00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:17.924
of other people will do to us.

00:18:17.924 --> 00:18:20.518
I've got news for you,
so listen carefully.

00:18:20.518 --> 00:18:22.841
I don't get on my soapbox
about many things,

00:18:22.841 --> 00:18:25.296
but I'm getting on it about this, guys.

00:18:25.296 --> 00:18:28.868
Nobody cares enough about you
to bother to give an opinion

00:18:28.868 --> 00:18:31.796
because they're too busy being
worried about what they think

00:18:31.796 --> 00:18:33.481
you're thinking of them.

00:18:33.481 --> 00:18:34.481
Failure?

00:18:34.481 --> 00:18:36.709
Failure is not taking your step.

00:18:36.709 --> 00:18:39.431
Failure is not picking up the
bat and swinging it at life.

00:18:39.431 --> 00:18:42.722
Failure is getting to the end of this game

00:18:42.722 --> 00:18:44.997
and regretting what we didn't do.

00:18:44.997 --> 00:18:47.842
Failure is about saying, "What if."

00:18:47.842 --> 00:18:49.779
Failure is lying on
your death bed thinking,

00:18:49.779 --> 00:18:52.613
"Oh, well, if I only I
could go back and do"

00:18:52.613 --> 00:18:53.844
fill-in-the-blank.

00:18:53.844 --> 00:18:54.677
You know something?

00:18:54.677 --> 00:18:57.052
To me, failure is not falling down,

00:18:57.052 --> 00:18:58.902
it's staying down when you've fallen.

00:18:58.902 --> 00:19:01.287
You have to fail by the definition of

00:19:01.287 --> 00:19:02.418
"Oh, I didn't succeed."

00:19:02.418 --> 00:19:04.584
in order so you can succeed.

00:19:04.584 --> 00:19:06.407
That's what life is about.

00:19:06.407 --> 00:19:08.277
It's not about taking
it with you at the end,

00:19:08.277 --> 00:19:09.701
it's not about score keeping.

00:19:09.701 --> 00:19:11.698
I've probably failed
more times than I've won,

00:19:11.698 --> 00:19:14.012
but I keep my average
number of tries high.

00:19:14.012 --> 00:19:15.405
And do you know what happens?

00:19:15.405 --> 00:19:16.636
Guess what?

00:19:16.636 --> 00:19:20.465
You tap into a lesson of
history that most people ignore.

00:19:20.465 --> 00:19:22.301
And that is this, it's
the paradox of history.

00:19:22.301 --> 00:19:24.680
For those that risk the least in life,

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:28.022
usually end up with the least in life.

00:19:28.022 --> 00:19:29.842
Just because our brain won't tell us that

00:19:29.842 --> 00:19:31.676
when we have to pay
our mortgage on Friday,

00:19:31.676 --> 00:19:33.474
doesn't mean it isn't true.

00:19:33.474 --> 00:19:35.008
So get up and get in the game.

00:19:35.008 --> 00:19:37.592
Who you are right now watching this

00:19:37.592 --> 00:19:40.678
is as a result of your
failures, not your successes.

00:19:40.678 --> 00:19:41.973
It is when we're tested,

00:19:41.973 --> 00:19:44.436
when the storm is ripping
the branches off our tree,

00:19:44.436 --> 00:19:47.476
when the rain cloud are there

00:19:47.476 --> 00:19:48.895
and we think we've got nothing left.

00:19:48.895 --> 00:19:50.460
That's who we are at our best,

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:52.330
when we show up when we're tested.

00:19:52.330 --> 00:19:55.546
The strongest trees grow
in the strongest winds,

00:19:55.546 --> 00:19:57.311
not in the best soil.

00:19:57.311 --> 00:19:59.068
So next time you have an opportunity,

00:19:59.068 --> 00:20:01.041
next time you start to question

00:20:01.041 --> 00:20:02.911
whether you should step forward or not,

00:20:02.911 --> 00:20:04.779
or would it be a white
square on the chess board,

00:20:04.779 --> 00:20:05.739
or a dark square or not?

00:20:05.739 --> 00:20:07.225
Who cares, get in the game,

00:20:07.225 --> 00:20:09.952
swing the bat, be all you can be.

00:20:09.952 --> 00:20:12.102
Get up, and if anybody says,
"Oh, you're doing that?"

00:20:12.102 --> 00:20:12.935
or "Oh, you did that?

00:20:12.935 --> 00:20:14.045
"Oh, look at, you failed."

00:20:14.045 --> 00:20:17.806
Know this, they're failing
in their judgement of you,

00:20:17.806 --> 00:20:21.470
not in your ability to pick
up the bat and swing it again.

00:20:21.470 --> 00:20:23.563
That's the person you were
born to be, my friends.

00:20:23.563 --> 00:20:25.365
That's the person who you are.

00:20:25.365 --> 00:20:27.548
You were born a miracle,
you are good enough.

00:20:27.548 --> 00:20:29.832
You don't need me to tell
you that, you already are.

00:20:29.832 --> 00:20:31.542
Get out there, get in the game,

00:20:31.542 --> 00:20:34.184
go embrace it, and if you
fall over, pick yourself up,

00:20:34.184 --> 00:20:35.559
swing the bat again.

00:20:35.559 --> 00:20:38.559
And let's go play this game of life.

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:41.632
- Thank you guys so much for watching,

00:20:41.632 --> 00:20:44.225
I made this video because
Kevin Lye asked me to.

00:20:44.225 --> 00:20:45.464
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:20:45.464 --> 00:20:46.886
that you want me to profile next,

00:20:46.886 --> 00:20:49.173
leave it in the comments below,
and I'll see what I can do.

00:20:49.173 --> 00:20:51.085
I'd also love to know what did Peter say

00:20:51.085 --> 00:20:52.598
that had the biggest impact on you

00:20:52.598 --> 00:20:54.132
in your business or your life?

00:20:54.132 --> 00:20:56.139
What change you're going to
make after watching this video.

00:20:56.139 --> 00:20:57.881
Please leave it in the comments,

00:20:57.881 --> 00:20:59.003
and I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:20:59.003 --> 00:21:01.514
Finally want to give a shout
out to Jaslin Purification.

00:21:01.514 --> 00:21:03.903
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book

00:21:03.903 --> 00:21:07.354
and making that awesome
Facebook art that you posted.

00:21:07.354 --> 00:21:09.177
I really, really, really appreciate it.

00:21:09.177 --> 00:21:10.627
So thank you guys, again, for watching.

00:21:10.627 --> 00:21:11.653
I believe in you.

00:21:11.653 --> 00:21:13.695
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:21:13.695 --> 00:21:15.914
and whatever your one word is.

00:21:15.914 --> 00:21:18.759
Much love, I'll see you soon.

00:21:18.759 --> 00:21:21.509
(exploding boom)

00:21:24.902 --> 00:21:28.609
- Determination, for me, is
far more important than desire.

00:21:28.609 --> 00:21:31.901
Desire comes from a place
of thinking I need it.

00:21:31.901 --> 00:21:34.397
Therefore, the presupposition
is "I'm not good enough,

00:21:34.397 --> 00:21:36.034
"because I don't already have it."

00:21:36.034 --> 00:21:38.495
Determination is simply a case of

00:21:38.495 --> 00:21:40.961
"Well, here's where I'm focused,
here's where I'm going."

00:21:40.961 --> 00:21:43.793
I don't need it, I'm
just choosing to get it.

00:21:43.793 --> 00:21:47.091
And get out of the damn
way, 'cause I'm moving.

00:21:47.091 --> 00:21:49.166
Questions direct our focus.

00:21:49.166 --> 00:21:52.070
And if you're not
directing your own focus,

00:21:52.070 --> 00:21:53.106
I've got news for you.

00:21:53.106 --> 00:21:54.959
There's a lot of people
that pay a lot of good money

00:21:54.959 --> 00:21:58.670
to Madison Avenue to figure
out how to do it for you.

00:21:58.670 --> 00:22:00.184
- [Evan] Right.

00:22:00.184 --> 00:22:02.055
- And that's not the
life you want to live,

00:22:02.055 --> 00:22:03.992
being programmed by
other people's agendas.

00:22:03.992 --> 00:22:07.545
And I liken the mind to a compass needle.

00:22:07.545 --> 00:22:11.018
It can only point in
one direction at a time.

00:22:11.018 --> 00:22:14.894
And the challenge is, just
like if we take a needle,

00:22:14.894 --> 00:22:17.150
and magnetize it like back in high school.

00:22:17.150 --> 00:22:20.052
You take a magnet, a power source,

00:22:20.052 --> 00:22:23.097
and you align it, and
keep stroking that needle

00:22:23.097 --> 00:22:26.131
in one continuous direction,
'til that needle aligns to

00:22:26.131 --> 00:22:28.615
the magnetic field, and becomes coherent,

00:22:28.615 --> 00:22:31.078
all of the ions pointing in one direction,

00:22:31.078 --> 00:22:32.323
it becomes magnetized.

00:22:32.323 --> 00:22:34.834
Our mind is very similar.

00:22:34.834 --> 00:22:38.876
If we are open to
unconsciously being programmed,

00:22:38.876 --> 00:22:40.869
which unfortunately as
human beings we are.

00:22:40.869 --> 00:22:45.006
We're a 24/7 constant adaptation machine,

00:22:45.006 --> 00:22:46.506
our mind our body.

00:22:47.503 --> 00:22:49.732
Now we understand the
body part, that's easy.

00:22:49.732 --> 00:22:51.797
The physical side of life everybody gets,

00:22:51.797 --> 00:22:54.673
because they have
experiential evidence of it.

00:22:54.673 --> 00:22:57.104
Now your body will adapt if
you put it in McDonald's,

00:22:57.104 --> 00:22:58.982
or if you put in the gym, it doesn't mind,

00:22:58.982 --> 00:23:01.567
it will adapt accordingly, that's its job.

00:23:01.567 --> 00:23:04.894
But our mind is far more
programmable, far quicker

00:23:04.894 --> 00:23:06.345
than our body.

00:23:06.345 --> 00:23:10.780
And if the magnet, the strong
force that's constantly

00:23:10.780 --> 00:23:14.573
magnetizing us, is usually
the media and our peer group.

00:23:14.573 --> 00:23:18.740
And if those two aren't
optimal, then we're going to be

00:23:20.401 --> 00:23:22.622
sucked along for the ride,

00:23:22.622 --> 00:23:26.511
and don't really magnetize
our true north for ourselves.

00:23:26.511 --> 00:23:29.489
So by asking better
questions, what it does

00:23:29.489 --> 00:23:32.124
it shifts the direction of that needle.

00:23:32.124 --> 00:23:34.263
Now the challenge is, you can only do that

00:23:34.263 --> 00:23:36.202
for 10% of the time that you're conscious,

00:23:36.202 --> 00:23:40.184
or sleeping, awake is how most
people are 90% of the time.

00:23:40.184 --> 00:23:41.717
That's why when we're driving to work,

00:23:41.717 --> 00:23:43.869
we can't remember the last
two remember kilometers

00:23:43.869 --> 00:23:45.176
on the freeway, (laughs) that will happen.

00:23:45.176 --> 00:23:48.784
But, now if we focus on
being able to magnetize

00:23:48.784 --> 00:23:50.572
or take charge of which direction

00:23:50.572 --> 00:23:52.014
that compass needle is pointing,

00:23:52.014 --> 00:23:54.587
we have a chance to start
reinventing ourselves.

00:23:54.587 --> 00:23:58.389
Because, otherwise, again,
you're going to be drifting,

00:23:58.389 --> 00:24:00.411
especially in that 90% of
time where we do things

00:24:00.411 --> 00:24:03.560
out of habit, unconsciously,
that compass needle

00:24:03.560 --> 00:24:06.695
drifts back to its
pre-conditioned magnetic north.

00:24:06.695 --> 00:24:08.761
Now most of the time,
that's doesn't serve us,

00:24:08.761 --> 00:24:10.874
whether it's media
condition, people condition,

00:24:10.874 --> 00:24:12.558
via society condition.

00:24:12.558 --> 00:24:15.100
Looking out of your window,
there's not many examples

00:24:15.100 --> 00:24:17.191
who we really want to emulate and become

00:24:17.191 --> 00:24:19.431
that surround us on on a day-to-day basis.

00:24:19.431 --> 00:24:21.566
There is a way, believe it or not,

00:24:21.566 --> 00:24:24.398
that you can actually be luckier,

00:24:24.398 --> 00:24:27.010
and it's far simpler than you realize,

00:24:27.010 --> 00:24:29.380
especially when you understand
some of the science,

00:24:29.380 --> 00:24:32.282
and biochemistry, and neurochemistry,

00:24:32.282 --> 00:24:34.221
as to what's really going on.

00:24:34.221 --> 00:24:37.054
And when I say lucky,
I'm talking about things

00:24:37.054 --> 00:24:39.887
just falling into place, seemingly so,

00:24:39.887 --> 00:24:42.223
or if you meet the right person,

00:24:42.223 --> 00:24:45.246
or the right deal lands on your plate,

00:24:45.246 --> 00:24:47.746
and a lot of this is actually,

00:24:49.367 --> 00:24:53.480
you're able to set this
up in a a way where

00:24:53.480 --> 00:24:55.663
the odds are more in your favor.

00:24:55.663 --> 00:24:57.207
Just like if you're in a casino,

00:24:57.207 --> 00:25:00.794
life for some people is
where you put enough quarters

00:25:00.794 --> 00:25:04.602
in the machine, and you may
get three cherries in a row,

00:25:04.602 --> 00:25:06.585
'cause there's so much going on in life,

00:25:06.585 --> 00:25:09.229
so many plates spinning simultaneously,

00:25:09.229 --> 00:25:11.917
that occasionally, yes,
you'll just be lucky

00:25:11.917 --> 00:25:14.390
and get three cherries
in a row, that happens.

00:25:14.390 --> 00:25:17.216
But, more often than not,
how do we stack the odds

00:25:17.216 --> 00:25:18.400
in our favor?

00:25:18.400 --> 00:25:20.231
Now if you go to the roulette table,

00:25:20.231 --> 00:25:21.872
and you're betting black and red,

00:25:21.872 --> 00:25:24.771
the house will always win over time.

00:25:24.771 --> 00:25:25.772
Why?

00:25:25.772 --> 00:25:27.445
Because it's just not 50/50.

00:25:27.445 --> 00:25:30.928
There's a loss a little
green option called zero,

00:25:30.928 --> 00:25:33.122
which stacks the odds
in the house's favor,

00:25:33.122 --> 00:25:35.700
yet a little bit more than 50%.

00:25:35.700 --> 00:25:38.250
So the mathematics is the
house will always win.

00:25:38.250 --> 00:25:41.176
You may get lucky, but the
house will always win over time.

00:25:41.176 --> 00:25:43.916
So how do you go from being a person

00:25:43.916 --> 00:25:45.543
spinning the wheel in life,

00:25:45.543 --> 00:25:48.504
hoping that it's going
to land on your color,

00:25:48.504 --> 00:25:52.798
versus becoming the house,
whereby every single time,

00:25:52.798 --> 00:25:55.132
over time, you know ultimately,

00:25:55.132 --> 00:25:57.175
things are going to
work out in your favor.

00:25:57.175 --> 00:25:59.227
Well, let me share with
you an incredible part

00:25:59.227 --> 00:26:02.236
of the human anatomy that
allows that to happen.

00:26:02.236 --> 00:26:05.290
It's called the reticular
activating system,

00:26:05.290 --> 00:26:06.973
and it's a part of the brain

00:26:06.973 --> 00:26:08.797
that has a very specific job to do,

00:26:08.797 --> 00:26:10.538
and it's usually misunderstood.

00:26:10.538 --> 00:26:12.535
But the reticular activating system

00:26:12.535 --> 00:26:16.610
is really the gatekeeper between conscious

00:26:16.610 --> 00:26:18.293
and the unconscious mind.

00:26:18.293 --> 00:26:21.626
And hit has a sway over what information

00:26:22.728 --> 00:26:24.887
it allows in from a sensory input.

00:26:24.887 --> 00:26:27.383
Now how do we make the
reticular activating system

00:26:27.383 --> 00:26:30.920
work for us, when we want to
be, quote, unquote, lucky.

00:26:30.920 --> 00:26:34.524
Well, we need to understand
that it does one job

00:26:34.524 --> 00:26:37.449
and one job only, primarily
for the purposes of this video.

00:26:37.449 --> 00:26:41.242
And that is it allows
in, to our conscious,

00:26:41.242 --> 00:26:43.719
information that falls
under two categories.

00:26:43.719 --> 00:26:47.109
One, is information that
can be harmful to us.

00:26:47.109 --> 00:26:50.696
And the other is information
that we vote on it

00:26:50.696 --> 00:26:51.833
being relevant.

00:26:51.833 --> 00:26:53.587
So, for example, let's
talk about the first

00:26:53.587 --> 00:26:56.648
type of information,
stuff that can be harmful.

00:26:56.648 --> 00:26:59.125
So we're driving along, and
we're somewhat unconscious,

00:26:59.125 --> 00:27:01.304
as most people are, in
what I call sleeping awake,

00:27:01.304 --> 00:27:03.498
which is why you tend to
drive to work on your day off,

00:27:03.498 --> 00:27:05.666
because you've done it so many
times, you're unconscious,

00:27:05.666 --> 00:27:07.652
you're moving forward just out of habit.

00:27:07.652 --> 00:27:12.517
But we tend to wake up just
as the car in front of us

00:27:12.517 --> 00:27:14.784
brakes a little early and snaps us out.

00:27:14.784 --> 00:27:16.828
That's because the
reticular activating system

00:27:16.828 --> 00:27:20.305
is constantly scanning for
something that could be danger.

00:27:20.305 --> 00:27:21.618
And it works in conjunction

00:27:21.618 --> 00:27:23.663
with another part of of the
brain called the amygdala,

00:27:23.663 --> 00:27:25.674
whose job is to really notice things

00:27:25.674 --> 00:27:27.983
that are negative or
dangerous, before positive.

00:27:27.983 --> 00:27:30.318
So the amygdala will notice that,

00:27:30.318 --> 00:27:31.920
flag it up to the reticular
activating system,

00:27:31.920 --> 00:27:33.985
bring it into your conscious awareness,

00:27:33.985 --> 00:27:36.945
while everything else, meanwhile,
is swept under the carpet.

00:27:36.945 --> 00:27:40.495
And the amygdala's a
fascinating part of the brain.

00:27:40.495 --> 00:27:43.949
As I say, if you're walking
past a tree, 10,000 years ago,

00:27:43.949 --> 00:27:46.101
and you miss an apple, no big deal.

00:27:46.101 --> 00:27:48.596
But if you miss a snake,
it could be a big deal.

00:27:48.596 --> 00:27:51.200
So it's always scanning in conjunction

00:27:51.200 --> 00:27:52.902
with the reticular activating system,

00:27:52.902 --> 00:27:54.980
to see if there's
anything in our awareness

00:27:54.980 --> 00:27:57.619
that could be dangerous, harmful,
or threaten us physically.

00:27:57.619 --> 00:28:01.572
So, in terms of the other information,

00:28:01.572 --> 00:28:04.069
what we tell it is important.

00:28:04.069 --> 00:28:06.489
Now here's where we start
getting interesting,

00:28:06.489 --> 00:28:07.847
when we talk about getting lucky.

00:28:07.847 --> 00:28:10.785
See, the reticular activating system will,

00:28:10.785 --> 00:28:11.954
as a faithful servant,

00:28:11.954 --> 00:28:15.022
irrespective of the nature
of the import, do its job.

00:28:15.022 --> 00:28:17.152
So if you, for example, our name,

00:28:17.152 --> 00:28:19.357
we know our name is important to us.

00:28:19.357 --> 00:28:22.272
So if we're at a party, and
we're having a conversation

00:28:22.272 --> 00:28:24.316
with somebody, and
there's lots of background

00:28:24.316 --> 00:28:25.452
conversations going on.

00:28:25.452 --> 00:28:27.264
But somebody at the other side of the room

00:28:27.264 --> 00:28:28.700
happens to mention our name.

00:28:28.700 --> 00:28:31.584
In mid-conversation, we will be pulled out

00:28:31.584 --> 00:28:35.101
and look over to see who mentioned
our name across the room,

00:28:35.101 --> 00:28:37.005
in the middle of another conversation.

00:28:37.005 --> 00:28:38.538
Why is that?

00:28:38.538 --> 00:28:40.616
It's because the reticular
activating system

00:28:40.616 --> 00:28:43.470
is constantly scanning
all of this information,

00:28:43.470 --> 00:28:47.488
and it's deleting, distorting,
and generalizing 99% of it.

00:28:47.488 --> 00:28:49.533
I say otherwise we'd be
completely overwhelmed.

00:28:49.533 --> 00:28:52.888
And it's sweeping that under
the carpet of our awareness,

00:28:52.888 --> 00:28:54.176
our conscious awareness,

00:28:54.176 --> 00:28:55.515
and just flagging up what's important.

00:28:55.515 --> 00:28:57.231
That's why we didn't hear
somebody else's name,

00:28:57.231 --> 00:28:58.756
but we would hear our name.

00:28:58.756 --> 00:29:03.029
So if we tell the
reticular activating system

00:29:03.029 --> 00:29:05.687
what is important, it
will go and find it in the

00:29:05.687 --> 00:29:08.869
millions of bytes and bits of information

00:29:08.869 --> 00:29:10.714
a second that's it being processed.

00:29:10.714 --> 00:29:12.987
So you could walk down the street

00:29:12.987 --> 00:29:15.428
and completely miss an opportunity,

00:29:15.428 --> 00:29:17.878
because you haven't told the
reticular activating system,

00:29:17.878 --> 00:29:21.140
or your brain, that it
is relevant or important,

00:29:21.140 --> 00:29:23.300
even though it's working up millions

00:29:23.300 --> 00:29:25.422
of pieces of information every second.

00:29:25.422 --> 00:29:27.417
Give you another example.

00:29:27.417 --> 00:29:28.906
If you had a six-year-old daughter,

00:29:28.906 --> 00:29:30.667
and she turns around and
says, "Daddy, daddy, please,

00:29:30.667 --> 00:29:32.118
"I would love a bike for birthday, please,

00:29:32.118 --> 00:29:33.087
"that's all I want is a bike."

00:29:33.087 --> 00:29:34.521
You know, "Okay, honey."

00:29:34.521 --> 00:29:37.581
And you to your wife, "I've got
to get our daughter a bike."

00:29:37.581 --> 00:29:39.653
And you're driving to work the next day,

00:29:39.653 --> 00:29:42.681
and then all of a sudden
you drive past a bike shop.

00:29:42.681 --> 00:29:44.606
And you notice a bike
shop on the way to work.

00:29:44.606 --> 00:29:46.793
Now it's been there for
the last five years,

00:29:46.793 --> 00:29:48.474
every day you've driven to work.

00:29:48.474 --> 00:29:51.437
You noticed it in your
reticular activating system,

00:29:51.437 --> 00:29:53.559
but because you haven't told
your brain it was important,

00:29:53.559 --> 00:29:55.627
it swept it under the carpet of awareness,

00:29:55.627 --> 00:29:57.718
and you didn't notice
it in your conscious.

00:29:57.718 --> 00:29:59.204
But now you've said it's relevant,

00:29:59.204 --> 00:30:01.682
so it pulls it out of
all of the information.

00:30:01.682 --> 00:30:02.948
Says, "Hey, guess what?"

00:30:02.948 --> 00:30:05.381
Wow, just the same as if you buy a car

00:30:05.381 --> 00:30:07.542
and you start seeing that
car everywhere on the road.

00:30:07.542 --> 00:30:08.898
Of course it was there before,

00:30:08.898 --> 00:30:10.813
there wasn't a half-price sale on it,

00:30:10.813 --> 00:30:12.775
now everybody's bought the same car.

00:30:12.775 --> 00:30:15.378
No, you've now told your
reticular activating system

00:30:15.378 --> 00:30:17.911
this particular car, make,
model, color, what have you,

00:30:17.911 --> 00:30:20.373
is now more relevant to me in my life

00:30:20.373 --> 00:30:23.009
and then out of the hundreds
or thousands of cars

00:30:23.009 --> 00:30:25.331
on the road, whenever it
spots one, as it always did,

00:30:25.331 --> 00:30:26.782
it will flag it up.

00:30:26.782 --> 00:30:28.499
Basic neuroscience.

00:30:28.499 --> 00:30:30.519
So how do we make that work for us?

00:30:30.519 --> 00:30:34.663
Well, if it's going to constantly, 24/7,

00:30:34.663 --> 00:30:37.932
look for all of the
information that is out there,

00:30:37.932 --> 00:30:40.265
that's beyond our conscious comprehension,

00:30:40.265 --> 00:30:44.347
or our ability to process
consciously, and start scanning,

00:30:44.347 --> 00:30:46.233
what a great opportunity that is.

00:30:46.233 --> 00:30:47.773
See, if I turn around and say,

00:30:47.773 --> 00:30:52.374
"Right now I'm looking
for a business partner.

00:30:52.374 --> 00:30:56.541
"I'm looking for a store, a
premises, a vacant premises.

00:30:59.289 --> 00:31:00.792
"I'm looking for certain
kind of property."

00:31:00.792 --> 00:31:03.047
And you say it's relevant,
you're going to start noticing

00:31:03.047 --> 00:31:04.903
things like that, while
you're driving along,

00:31:04.903 --> 00:31:06.834
in the process of normal conversations,

00:31:06.834 --> 00:31:08.505
when you're standing in
a line up at Starbucks,

00:31:08.505 --> 00:31:10.712
overhearing somebody talk about a business

00:31:10.712 --> 00:31:11.814
that's relevant to you,

00:31:11.814 --> 00:31:13.475
because you're telling it its important.

